course: dictionary
lesson: 2658
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word developer is a good example. «Technology changes fast; many jobs today, like app developer or social media manager, did not exist 30 years ago.» Here a developer is a person who writes computer programs and apps.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. A property developer buys land and builds houses, shops or offices on it. Look at the words around it: apps, games and code point to computers, while land, houses and offices point to buildings.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «Game developer» is not one job but many: programmer, artist, animator, sound designer, writer, tester and producer. So the word can stand for a whole team of people, not just one job.
fact: Developer is a noun, and developers is its plural.
fact: «Developer» means a person or company that writes computer programs, apps or games.
fact: «Developer» can also mean a person or company that buys land and builds houses, shops or offices on it.
fact: In old-style photography, a developer was a chemical that made photos appear on film or paper.
fact: «Developer» can also mean someone who develops or works out a new idea or product.
exercise: «Technology changes fast; many jobs today, like app developer, did not exist 30 years ago.» What is an app developer? | Someone who sells fruit at the market | *Someone who writes apps for phones and computers | Someone who fixes cars | Someone who paints houses
exercise: Ravi reads «property developer» in the news about new flats. What does it mean? | A chemical used for photos | A person who teaches dance | *A person who buys land and builds houses or shops on it | A person who sells newspapers
exercise: «The old developer liquid brought the pictures out on the film.» What is the developer in this sentence? | A bottle of dance music | A person who takes photos at a wedding | A type of camera | *A chemical used to make photos appear
test: «A game developer is not one job but many: programmer, artist, animator, sound designer.» What does game developer mean? | A teacher of maths | *A company or person who makes games | A person who plays games for fun | A shop that sells toys
test: «Our town will get a new shopping centre built by a developer.» Which meaning fits? | A person who writes computer games | *Someone who buys land and builds shops on it | A sweet made with honey | Someone who has a sore throat
exam: Ellie reads «developer» in three sentences about apps, land and photos. What should she do to find each meaning? | *Read the words around it, then swap in each meaning to see which fits | Look only at the first letter of the word | Skip the word and never read the sentence again | Always guess the most common meaning, every time
